-old dogs.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - Chihuahua mixes: Audrey has two Chihuahua mixes named Precious and Pixie. She consulted an animal behaviorist due to her dogs not acting normally.\n  - other pups: The dogs of Audrey love Fetch and Frisbee and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - blanket: Audrey shared a picture of her four dogs snuggling on her favorite blanket.\n  - pet store: Audrey went to a pet store last Monday to buy toys for her dogs.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - four pups: Audrey's four pups enjoy many activities, including puzzles, training, and hide-and-seek. Audrey meets with a dog owners group weekly for tips and playdates.\n  - puzzles: Audrey's four pups enjoy many activities, including puzzles, training, and hide-and-seek.\n  - dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon; they looked cute, groomed, and had shiny coats. Andrew has two dogs, Toby and Buddy. They are considered family members.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - friends: Audrey meets with other dog owners weekly for tips and playdates for her four pups. Andrew values friends for support, and Audrey values friendship.\n  - doggo: Audrey groomed her dogs, who looked cute with shiny coats after being good at the salon. Andrew adopted another dog and shared a photo.\n  - frisbee: Audrey's dogs love to run around and meet other pups, and they go crazy for Fetch and Frisbee.\n  - tails: Audrey organized a doggy playdate where the sight of many wagging tails brought joy to her.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - pet salon: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; the dogs were excited, looked cute, and behaved well.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - pic of them after the grooming: Audrey learned grooming her pups herself, making her closer to them. Andrew requested a photo of the pups after the grooming to see how adorable they look.\n  - the doggos: Audrey takes the doggos for walks in the park to relax and clear her mind, as they offer a nature environment.\n  - vet trip: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic. She plans to take them one by one next time.\n  - neighbors' dogs: Audrey organized a doggy playdate with the neighbors' dogs, and seeing them wag their tails was sweet.\n  - rewards: Audrey is looking forward to learning how to train her pets better and believes they will learn quickly because they love rewards.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1973,"context_chars":7470,"retrieval_duration":0.18448233604431152,"response_dur