red a picture of his old gaming setup. John called the picture wonderful and mentioned showing it to elementary school friends. James praised The Witcher 3 in relation to the picture.\n  - James: James created a game, inspired by Witcher 3, and was fulfilled seeing players engage. He recently adopted a pup named Ned from a Stamford shelter and organized an online programming competition with John.\n  - John: John found the pets in James's picture cute, felt love and joy from the photo, and started thinking about his future.\n  - programming projects: John asked James about what motivates him for programming projects; James later worked on a virtual world inspired by Witcher 3 with a gaming pal.\n  - John: John plays drums, recently chatted with James about a new RPG with a cool story and tough gameplay, which sometimes causes lag and errors.\n  - another world: James mentioned that gaming helps him forget life's stresses by transporting him to \"another world\". He and a gaming pal later created a virtual world inspired by Witcher 3 using programming.\n  - gaming pal: James worked on a programming project with a gaming pal last Thursday, creating a virtual world inspired by Witcher 3.\n  - John: John expressed that losing power during a game is a bummer and asked James to see a picture of him playing on an old gaming setup.\n  - John: John empathized with James about losing power during a game. John stated a seminar he led went well, featuring a great turnout and knowledge sharing.\n  - James: James chatted with John about work and asked what games John was playing.\n  - John: John expressed empathy to James about losing power during a game and later asked James about his mother's friend possibly still being in the army.\n  - John: John is communicating with James, expressing sympathy about James losing power mid-game and asking if it affected his progress.\n  - John: John commiserated with James about losing power during a game and offered to send him resources and