ject was inspired by a San Francisco car workshop visit and brings satisfaction when people see the finished product.\n  - working on cars: Dave enjoys working on cars, as music helps him focus and feel great while doing it. Calvin finds repairing things fulfilling, similar to Dave's satisfaction with car work.\n  - Dave: Dave is fascinated by how machines work, starting at age ten after fixing an old car. He enjoys car engineering and transforming broken-down vehicles into high-running ones.\n  - Dave: Dave attended a car workshop in San Francisco to learn car restoration techniques. He also had a card night with friends last Friday and discussed his ongoing car restoration project with Calvin.\n  - Dave: Dave, who is restoring a vintage Mustang engine, has taken up photography, focusing on local scenery. He discussed his photography and the car project with Calvin.\n  - Dave: Dave previously enjoyed a card night and is restoring a car for his auto engineering goal. He chatted with Calvin about Calvin's amazing performance on a big stage.\n  - Dave: Dave recently returned from San Francisco with insights on car modification, finding satisfaction in fixing and improving old cars to help others.\n  - cars: Dave shared a picture of his latest car project, which Calvin found inspiring, contrasting it with Calvin's music endeavors. Dave finds working on cars therapeutic.\n  - car maintenance shop: Dave's car maintenance shop lost a deal they pursued for months to a competing shop, making Dave feel bummed out despite his hard work.\n  - engineer: Dave became an engineer and works on car projects, which Calvin finds inspiring for his music career.\n  - junkyard: Dave found a Ford Mustang in a junkyard; the car was in bad shape but had potential for restoration.\n  - Dave: Dave's band had a fun rehearsal session last night. Last weekend, Dave attended a rock concert in Boston. Dave is also praised by Calvin for fixing cars.\n  - car stuff: Dave is tied up with car stuff, r