\n  - close friends: Caroline stated that some close friends kept supporting her, but a few were unable to handle a situation, though her current relationships feel more genuine.\n  - Family moments: Caroline values family moments, describing them as awesome and special, especially when spent with loved ones.\n  - support: Caroline values support from friends and family, and now aims to give back by offering comfort and help to others, similar to her past gratifying experience volunteering at an LGBTQ+ youth center.\n  - advocacy: Caroline plans to attend a transgender conference this month to learn more about advocacy and meet others in the community.\n  - moments: Melanie stated that playing games, eating good food, and hanging out constitute awesome family moments. She is glad Caroline is there to share in these special moments.\n  - relationships: Caroline's relationships changed; some friends couldn't handle it, but she is happier with those who accept and love her, leading to more genuine connections.\n  - people who embrace and back me up: Caroline stated that being around people who embrace and back her up was beyond words and really inspired her.\n  - my own journey: Caroline shared details of her transgender journey, including struggles and development since coming out and starting transition three years ago, at a school event to inspire others.\n  - family: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday, moving closer to her goal of building a family by providing a home and love to kids who need it through adoption.\n  - mentee: Caroline's mentee's face lit up when they saw the support, which was described as a special moment by Caroline.\n  - positive strategies: Caroline mentors a transgender teen, and they are working on building confidence and finding positive strategies.\n  - mentoring: Caroline finds the mentoring program rewarding, supporting amazing, resilient, and strong young folks; the experience is going great.\n  - milestones: Caroline mentioned that milestones are great reminders of how special the bonds between her and Mel are.\n  - council meeting for adoption: Caroline attended a council meeting for adoption last Friday; it was inspiring, emotional, and reinforced her determination to adopt.\n  - support groups: Caroline was inspired by counseling and support groups that improved her life, now motivating her to help others through similar services.\n  - Caroline: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday. She is excited to build a family by adopting needy kids, viewing adoption as a way to give back, show love, and acceptance.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1960,"context_chars":8260,"retrieval_duration":0.1643204689025879,"response_duration":2.6505744457244873,"total_duration":2.814894914627075,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer specifies a date (June 2, 2023) that falls within the week before June 9, 2023, thus addressing the same time period as the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides specific information that Caroline met up with her friends, family, and mentors last week, which corresponds to the date of 9 June 2023. This aligns perfectly with the golden answer, confirming that all necessary details are present to answer the question.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Caroline met up with her friends last week.","Caroline met up with her mentors last week.","Caroline met up with her family last week."]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_1","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_1_qa_49","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What did Gina want her customers to feel in her store?","golden_answer":"cozy and comfortable","hypothesis":"Gina wanted her customers to feel cozy and like they are in a cool oasis in her store. She designed the space to reflect her own style and aimed to create a special shopping experience that would make customers want to return.","context