d help. Calvin recently toured with Frank Ocean.\n  - studio: Calvin's music studio was complimented by Dave. Calvin recorded a song with Frank Ocean there after meeting at a Tokyo music festival; it also has a cozy relaxation room.\n  - new sounds: Calvin is having fun trying out new sounds and pushing boundaries, always seeking new ideas to stay ahead.\n  - music: Calvin and an artist discussed favorite artists, art, and music's power to connect people, leading to a creative high for Calvin. Dave also noted music fosters creativity.\n  - helpful people: Calvin values supportive people for artist development and motivation, recalling how relationships sparked feelings similar to when he and friends freestyled as teenagers.\n  - high school friend: Calvin invited his high school friend to see him perform in Boston. The friend's presence made Calvin feel nostalgic about freestyling days, and his support helps Calvin's music career.\n  - musicians: Calvin performed in Boston and is now supporting ambitious young musicians, viewing it as passing the torch to keep music alive.\n  - Dave: Dave asked Calvin about his car post-crash, mentioned arranging regular walks with friends in parks, and commented on a mansion's stunning view in Japan.\n  - the boys: Calvin performed with 'the boys' last night and stated they are great at music.\n  - team: Calvin mentioned his team is part of his strong support system that helps him manage his overwhelming job demands. He was also with his crew at a fancy gala in Boston.\n  - Cal: Calvin (Cal) works with new talent, making a beat for a young artist with great music potential. He enjoys seeing his old friends who support him.\n  - touring: Calvin started touring with Frank Ocean and is enjoying the amazing energy and connection on stage during performances.\n  - creative haven: Calvin refers to his 'creative haven' as the place where he pours his heart into music, following a flood incident.\n  - fanbase: Calvin attended a networking 