ation and checking out career options, which she finds exciting.\n  - my own struggles: Caroline's past struggles made her feel alone, and sharing her story while volunteering at an LGBTQ+ youth center helped her support others.\n  - counselor: Melanie thinks Caroline would be a great counselor due to her empathy and understanding.\n  - people who embrace and back me up: Caroline stated that being around people who embrace and back her up was beyond words and really inspired her.\n  - mentee: Caroline's mentee's face lit up when they saw the support, which was described as a special moment by Caroline.\n  - support and encouragement: Caroline appreciated Melanie's support and encouragement regarding her talk on her transgender journey, which aimed to inspire others and promote inclusivity.\n  - support network: Caroline stated her support network has been amazing, providing love, guidance, and acceptance to help her through tough times.\n  - empathy and understanding: Melanie noted that Caroline's empathy and understanding would make her a great counselor, helping people she works with.\n  - mentors: Caroline is thankful for her mentors' support, which inspires her to keep making art.\n  - LGBTQ+ counseling workshop: Caroline attended an LGBTQ+ counseling workshop last Friday about therapeutic methods for working with and supporting the mental health of trans people.\n  - self-acceptance: Caroline stated that finding self-acceptance was a long process, but now she is ready to offer love and support, feeling empowered to make a positive difference.\n  - courage to transition: Caroline stated that realizing she could be herself without fear and having the courage to transition was the best part, calling it freeing to express herself authentically with support.\n  - my own journey: Caroline shared details of her transgender journey, including struggles and development since coming out and starting transition three years ago, at a school event to inspire others.\n  - lo